6.22:
When you walk, they will guide you;
when you lie down, they will watch over you;
when you awake, they will speak to you.

7.2:
Keep my commandments and live;
guard my teachings as the apple
of your eye.

9.1:
Wisdom has built her house;
she has carved out
her seven pillars.

18.10:
The name of the LORD is a strong tower;
the righteous run to it
and are safe.

20.19:
He who reveals secrets is a constant gossip;
avoid the one who babbles
with his lips.

22.29:
Do you see a man skilled in his work?
He will be stationed in the presence of kings;
he will not stand before obscure men.

25.13:
Like the cold of snow in the time of harvest
is a trustworthy messenger to those who send him;
he refreshes the soul of his masters.

27.20:
Sheol and Abaddon
are never satisfied;
so the eyes of man are never satisfied.

30.8:
Keep falsehood and deceitful words far from me.
Give me neither poverty nor riches;
feed me with the bread that is my portion.

